  "term": "neurotransmitter",
  "definition": "A neurotransmitter is a naturally produced signaling chemical that changes the activity of neurons or other target cells. In the broad sense, it includes substances that act directly on ion channels, work through second-messenger pathways, or influence cells at some distance from where they are released, including effects outside synapses.",
